    <entry>
        <title>Kiva Systems / Amazon Robotics</title>
        <author>
            <name>Rob Brown</name>
        </author>
        <link href="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/kiva-systems-amazon-robotics/"/>
        <id>https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/kiva-systems-amazon-robotics/</id>
        <media:content url="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/20130222_11-11-03.jpg" medium="image" />

        <updated>2026-09-19T20:00:00-04:00</updated>
            <summary type="html">
                <![CDATA[
                        <img src="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/20130222_11-11-03.jpg" alt="" />
                    I was on the founding product team at Kiva Systems, building the robotic warehouse systems that Amazon acquired for $775M, which became the backbone of Amazon Robotics. I helped scale that technology across Amazon's fulfillment network: cutting costs, deploying new robotics systems, and increasing performance&hellip;
                ]]>
            </summary>
        <content type="html">
            <![CDATA[
                    <p><img src="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/20130222_11-11-03.jpg" class="type:primaryImage" alt="" /></p>
                <p><span style="font-weight: 400;">I was on the founding product team at Kiva Systems, building the robotic warehouse systems that Amazon acquired for $775M, which became the backbone of Amazon Robotics. I helped scale that technology across Amazon's fulfillment network: cutting costs, deploying new robotics systems, and increasing performance (1M+ bots deployed globally today). We succeeded with a low ego, high execution team, inspired and trusted to deliver. I led a team of product managers, mechanical engineers, and TPMs.</span></p>
<p><strong>Product Manager,</strong><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Kiva Systems (pre Amazon.com acquisition)</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">2010 – 2012</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Requirements and human-machine interface design for pioneering warehouse robotics solution.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Direct engagement / boots on ground  with customers including Diapers.com, The Gap for product feedback.</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-is-empty="false" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="2">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/kivacommercial.png" data-size="1244x727"><img loading="lazy" src="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/kivacommercial-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="449"></a>
<figcaption>Kiva System in customer warehouse - pre Amazon Acquisition</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/kivaamazon.png" data-size="1174x659"><img loading="lazy" src="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/kivaamazon-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="431"></a>
<figcaption>Kiva deployment in Amazon Fulfillment Center</figcaption>
</figure>
</div></div>
<p><strong>Senior Technical Product Manager,</strong><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Amazon Robotics</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">2012 – 2013</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Design and development of Amazon’s first Kiva-enabled robotics fulfillment centers. Customer: Amazon Global Operations.</span></li>
</ul>
<figure class="post__video"><iframe loading="lazy" width="600" height="336" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Jh27vjAhE-c" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen" data-mce-fragment="1"></iframe></figure>
<p><strong>Product Management and TPM Team Lead,</strong><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Automation &amp; Robotics Advanced Programs (XB-15)</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">2013 – 2017</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Next-gen warehouse robotics and automation including Kiva Systems robotics, AS&amp;RS and robotic arms. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Solution design &amp; deployment of full scale building automation (1M sq ft), and hands-on support through peak operations.</span></li>
</ul>
<div class="gallery-wrapper"><div class="gallery" data-is-empty="false" data-translation="Add images" data-columns="2">
<figure class="gallery__item"><a href="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/amazonbdl1.png" data-size="1075x604"><img loading="lazy" src="https://brownphotographic.github.io/rb-web/media/posts/6/gallery/amazonbdl1-thumbnail.png" alt="" width="768" height="432"></a>
